From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: nss: unlink only the freed vap from mesh_vaps

ath11k_nss_mesh_vdev_free() should drop the vap it frees from the global
mesh_vaps list, but it walks the list and unlinks every entry. With mesh
on two radios, taking one down also drops the other radio's link vap,
which is still in use. dbg_infra/links then lists only the re-created
link, and nss_mesh/dbg_infra/assoc_link fails for the other one with
"unable to find if_num".

Seen on IPQ5018 + QCN6122 with a mesh interface on each radio: after
`wifi up radio1`, links showed only radio1's new link id; radio0's link
was gone while its mesh interface stayed up.

mesh_vaps only backs that debug tooling, so the data path is unaffected.

Unlink only this vap's own entry. list_del_init() keeps a second unlink
harmless.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -2597,7 +2597,7 @@
 	struct ath11k *ar = arvif->ar;
 	struct ath11k_nss_mpath_entry *mpath_entry, *mpath_tmp;
 	struct ath11k_nss_mpp_entry *mpp_entry, *mpp_tmp;
-	struct arvif_nss *nss = &arvif->nss, *nss_entry, *nss_tmp;
+	struct arvif_nss *nss = &arvif->nss;
 	LIST_HEAD(mpath_local_entry);
 	LIST_HEAD(mpp_local_entry);
 	nss_tx_status_t status;
@@ -2622,8 +2622,7 @@
 		kfree(mpp_entry);
 	}
 
-	list_for_each_entry_safe(nss_entry, nss_tmp, &mesh_vaps, list)
-		list_del(&nss_entry->list);
+	list_del_init(&nss->list);
 
 	status = nss_dynamic_interface_dealloc_node(
 						arvif->nss.if_num,
